window.SITE_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"t":"3D models","s":"Opening a model","u":"deep/3d-models.html#opening-a-model","l":"deep","x":"Models open in the 3D studio viewer: .glb , .gltf , .obj , .fbx , .stl and .ply directly, and .usd , .usda , .usdc , .usdz , .abc and .blend after a background conversion. See USD and Alembic for the conversion. A gem model in the studio viewer. The panel in the bottom left shows the mesh statistics."},{"t":"3D models","s":"Moving the camera","u":"deep/3d-models.html#moving-the-camera","l":"deep","x":"Drag with the left button to orbit, the right button to pan and the wheel to zoom. F frames the model. The numpad keys snap to views: 1 front, 3 right, 7 top, and Ctrl with 1 or 3 for the back or left side. 5 switches between perspective and orthographic. The camera menu sets the focal length (18, 35, 50, 85 and 200 mm) and the free or fixed view. Left-drag to orbit. The model stays framed."},{"t":"3D models","s":"Shading","u":"deep/3d-models.html#shading","l":"deep","x":"The shading list has the full PBR material, clay, wireframe, normal-map and matcap looks. Wireframe and grid buttons sit beside it. Clay and matcap modes show form and surface flow without colour, which is useful for checking dents and smooth curves."},{"t":"3D models","s":"Lights and the turntable","u":"deep/3d-models.html#lights-and-the-turntable","l":"deep","x":"The lighting list sets the studio rig: the softbox, sunset, neutral and cyber presets. The Light slider turns the light rig around the model. Turntable spins the model at an adjustable speed for a quick look from every side."},{"t":"3D models","s":"Animation","u":"deep/3d-models.html#animation","l":"deep","x":"Rigged models with animation clips show playback controls, so you can play, pause and scrub through a clip."},{"t":"3D models","s":"Statistics and snapshot","u":"deep/3d-models.html#statistics-and-snapshot","l":"deep","x":"The statistics panel shows the number of vertices, triangles, meshes and materials and the model's size. Snapshot saves what you see as a PNG. You choose where the file goes."},{"t":"3D models","s":"The outliner","u":"deep/3d-models.html#the-outliner","l":"deep","x":"Press O to open the outliner, which lists the parts of the scene. Click a part to select it and frame it. The USD and Alembic page has an example."},{"t":"Architecture notes for contributors","s":"The parts","u":"deep/architecture.html#the-parts","l":"deep","x":"React 19 screens in src/ (Vite builds them). src/App.jsx holds the folder state and the routing between the grid and the viewers. Components live in src/components/ , helpers in src/utils/ . Bridge in src/tauriBridge.js . It gives the screens a window.electronAPI object and turns each call into a Tauri invoke . Screens never call Tauri directly. Rust backend in src-tauri/src/ . It reads folders, decodes thumbnails and EXR, manages network shares and file labels, and starts Blender. Each command is listed in the IPC table in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md . User guide in docs/site/ . src-tauri/build.rs lists its files and src-tauri/src/user_guide.rs embeds them in the program, so the installed app and the portable exe both carry the guide. The Help button saves a copy to docs/<version>/ in the app data folder (a new app version saves a fresh copy and removes the old one) and opens its index.html in the default browser. Blender runs headless from scripts/blender_convert.py for USD, Alembic and Blender files and for the optional studio thumbnails."},{"t":"Architecture notes for contributors","s":"Speed choices","u":"deep/architecture.html#speed-choices","l":"deep","x":"File listings are read on a worker thread and use directory metadata, so folders with thousands of files stay responsive. Thumbnails are decoded in Rust with a limit on how many run at once, and cached on disk by a hash of the path, size and modified time. Binary files travel as raw buffers rather than base64, so large textures are not copied through JSON. The grid is virtualised: only the visible cards are drawn."},{"t":"Architecture notes for contributors","s":"Keeping the guide and the app in step","u":"deep/architecture.html#keeping-the-guide-and-the-app-in-step","l":"deep","x":"The keyboard card in this guide is built from src/utils/shortcutList.js . When a key changes in a handler, change it in that list too. The list says which handler each group mirrors."},{"t":"Architecture notes for contributors","s":"Building the app","u":"deep/architecture.html#building-the-app","l":"deep","x":"npm install npm run tauri:dev # run the app npm run tauri:build # build the Windows installer and portable exe npm run version:check # the version must match in package.json, tauri.conf.json and Cargo.toml Versions follow semantic versioning. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md has the rules and the release steps."},{"t":"Architecture notes for contributors","s":"Building this guide","u":"deep/architecture.html#building-this-guide","l":"deep","x":"The guide's Markdown is in docs/site-src/content/ . The build writes plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript into docs/site/ : node docs/site-src/build.mjs The build needs only Node. It stops with a list of problems when a page links to a missing page or anchor, or to a picture that is not in docs/site/assets/media/ . The generated files are committed, so nobody needs Node to read the guide. See docs/site-src/README.md for how to add a page or replace a picture."},{"t":"Batch converter","s":"Converting","u":"deep/batch-converter.html#converting","l":"deep","x":"Select the images, right-click one of them, and choose Convert… . The dialog asks for the format and the output folder. The folder defaults to a converted folder next to each file. Press Convert and the work runs in the background. You can cancel a running job. Pick the format and where the converted files go"},{"t":"Batch converter","s":"Formats","u":"deep/batch-converter.html#formats","l":"deep","x":"PNG JPG TIFF BMP TGA WebP (lossless)"},{"t":"Batch converter","s":"Which files can be converted","u":"deep/batch-converter.html#which-files-can-be-converted","l":"deep","x":"PNG, JPG, JPEG, WebP, BMP, TGA, TIF, TIFF, HDR and EXR files can be converted. Other files are left out of the selection, and the menu item only appears when at least one file in the selection can be converted."},{"t":"Batch converter","s":"Existing files","u":"deep/batch-converter.html#existing-files","l":"deep","x":"The converter never overwrites a file. If a converted name already exists, it adds a number to the new name instead."},{"t":"Compare","s":"Choosing A and B","u":"deep/compare.html#choosing-a-and-b","l":"deep","x":"Each card has an A and a B button. Press one and the file is put into that slot; a file can be in only one slot. The compare bar at the bottom of the folder shows what is in each slot. Compare opens the comparison, and the cross removes a slot. The swap button turns A into B and B into A. Slot A and slot B, with the Compare button"},{"t":"Compare","s":"The four modes","u":"deep/compare.html#the-four-modes","l":"deep","x":"The modes sit in the top bar of the comparison, and the keys 1 to 4 pick them: Wipe ( 1 ): a divider runs down the middle. Drag it to show more of A or B. Side by side ( 2 ): both pictures are shown next to each other. A/B toggle ( 3 ): the picture switches between A and B in place. Space also switches between A and B. Diff ( 4 ): shows where the two pictures differ. Wipe mode: drag the divider to compare the same spot in A and B The comparison view in wipe mode. The labels at the top show the file names and sizes."},{"t":"Compare","s":"Zoom and pan","u":"deep/compare.html#zoom-and-pan","l":"deep","x":"Pan and zoom move both pictures together, so the same spot stays in view for each. R resets the view. Use it when a comparison has drifted."},{"t":"Compare","s":"Video and 3D","u":"deep/compare.html#video-and-3d","l":"deep","x":"Two videos compare the same way. X switches between A and B, Space plays and pauses, and the arrow keys step one frame ( Shift with an arrow steps one second). Two 3D models compare in the same window, and F frames them. > Note: For 3D models the fourth key (diff) does nothing."},{"t":"Folders and network drives","s":"Drives and the sidebar","u":"deep/folders-and-network.html#drives-and-the-sidebar","l":"deep","x":"The top of the sidebar lists your drives with their free space. Mapped network drives such as Z: appear next to local ones. Below them are four lists: Network locations : shares you typed in, plus the network places Windows Explorer already knows. Typed shares can be removed with the cross on their row. Recent folders : the last folders you opened, newest first. Folders that are offline are kept and come back when their share does. Pinned folders : folders you starred (the star on a folder row). Click the star again to unpin. Starred assets : files you starred from their card. The bottom of the sidebar counts the files in the current folder by type, and shows whether Blender was found."},{"t":"Folders and network drives","s":"The path bar","u":"deep/folders-and-network.html#the-path-bar","l":"deep","x":"Click a crumb to jump up the path, or the empty part of the bar (or press Ctrl + L ) to type a path. The app accepts Windows paths such as D:\\Projects , and network paths such as \\\\mypc\\library or //mypc/library . Use Alt + Left and Alt + Right , or the mouse side buttons, to go back and forward. Backspace goes up one folder. A folder is remembered per session. When you leave a viewer with Esc , you return to the folder you came from."},{"t":"Folders and network drives","s":"Filter, type filter and sorting","u":"deep/folders-and-network.html#filter-type-filter-and-sorting","l":"deep","x":"Ctrl + F puts the cursor in the filter box. Type part of a name and the folder shows only matches. The type buttons next to it limit the view to 3D, HDR, images, video, audio, PDF or Markdown files. Use the Name button in the path bar to sort by name, date modified, size or type, with folders first if you like. Click a column heading in the details view. The sort is remembered for each folder. Thumbnails. Ctrl + mouse wheel changes their size in the large icons view."},{"t":"Folders and network drives","s":"Selecting and changing the view","u":"deep/folders-and-network.html#selecting-and-changing-the-view","l":"deep","x":"Selection works as it does in File Explorer. Click selects one item. Ctrl + Click adds or removes one. Shift + Click selects a range, and Shift + arrow keys extend the selection from the anchor. Dragging on empty space draws a box. Home and End jump to the first and last item. The list icon in the path bar switches to the details view: name, date modified, type and size. Thumbnails in the large icons view can be made larger or smaller with Ctrl + mouse wheel, from 120 to 500 pixels. The size is remembered for each folder. Details view for the same folder Press F5 or Ctrl + R to refresh a folder in place. The selection and the view stay as they are."},{"t":"Folders and network drives","s":"Network shares","u":"deep/folders-and-network.html#network-shares","l":"deep","x":"Type a share in the path bar, for example \\\\studio\\library , and press Enter . The share is then listed in the sidebar (up to ten are kept). Slow or offline shares never freeze the app; they are listed as offline until they answer. Some shares refuse the Windows sign-in that File Explorer used. The app then shows an error that starts with a sign-in message. Click the + next to Network locations, enter the user name and password, and tick Remember if you want the share to reconnect every time the app starts. The password is kept in Windows Credential Manager, not in the app's settings file. Tip: If a share opens in File Explorer but not here, sign in with the + button once. A sign-in saved for one share on a PC is reused for the other shares on the same server."},{"t":"Folders and network drives","s":"Folder icons","u":"deep/folders-and-network.html#folder-icons","l":"deep","x":"Folders you customised in File Explorer keep their icon here. To change one, right-click the folder and choose Change icon… . Pick an icon from the library, which is made for CG and VFX work (3D, texturing, HDRIs, animation, media, scripts and more), or import your own PNG, SVG, ICO, WebP or JPG file of up to 2 MB. Choosing the default icon again resets the folder. Your choices are kept in the app's settings, so they also appear in the portable version."},{"t":"HDR and EXR maps","s":"Opening a map","u":"deep/hdr-exr.html#opening-a-map","l":"deep","x":".hdr and .exr files open in the HDR and EXR inspector. The map appears as a 360° sky that you can look around in. Use the flat view button in the toolbar to see the whole equirectangular image at once. The app reads 32-bit float values, so bright sun pixels keep their real brightness until you tone-map them. The sky on the left is the map as a dome. Controls sit in the panel on the right."},{"t":"HDR and EXR maps","s":"Exposure and tone mapping","u":"deep/hdr-exr.html#exposure-and-tone-mapping","l":"deep","x":"Exposure runs from −10 to +10 EV. Hold E and drag left or right, or use the slider. 0 resets it, and while E is held + and - step by half a stop. Tone mapping decides how the bright values are squeezed onto the screen. The list includes ACES, AgX, Cineon, Linear and Reinhard. Linear shows the raw values, which is the honest choice for checking light levels."},{"t":"HDR and EXR maps","s":"Channels","u":"deep/hdr-exr.html#channels","l":"deep","x":"Press 1 to 6 to solo a channel, such as red, green, blue, alpha or luminance, and C to cycle. A channel that is all black or all white tells you a lot about a pass before you look at the image."},{"t":"HDR and EXR maps","s":"Eyedropper and probes","u":"deep/hdr-exr.html#eyedropper-and-probes","l":"deep","x":"Hover over the map to read the linear RGB value of a pixel, the hex colour and the luminance. Click to pin the reading. Press P to show or hide the probes, the small markers that show where you sampled."},{"t":"HDR and EXR maps","s":"Other controls","u":"deep/hdr-exr.html#other-controls","l":"deep","x":"Z and drag zooms the view. 0 resets the zoom and F fits the view. V flips the image vertically, which helps when a map comes from a tool with the other convention. W turns the wipe on and off, to compare the map with another one. The panel lists the metadata of the file, the render passes (AOVs) inside an EXR, and the highlight roll-off setting. Tip: Large multi-layer EXR files take longer the first time because every layer is decoded. The result is cached, so the next visit is quick. See Troubleshooting ."},{"t":"Image sequences","s":"What counts as a sequence","u":"deep/image-sequences.html#what-counts-as-a-sequence","l":"deep","x":"A sequence is a set of frames with the same name and a number that goes up, such as beauty.0001.png , beauty.0002.png and so on. Renders are often written this way. The frames stay separate in the folder view, so you can still see and select each one. Each frame is a card, so you can still pick out a single frame"},{"t":"Image sequences","s":"Playing a sequence","u":"deep/image-sequences.html#playing-a-sequence","l":"deep","x":"Right-click any frame and choose Play as sequence . The player shows the frames in order. Use it to check motion, flicker and missing frames before you hand a render on. The player shows the frames in order. Its bar shows the frame number. Tip: A gap in the numbers is a missing frame. Look for it in the frame counter before you trust a render."},{"t":"Images and textures","s":"What opens here","u":"deep/images.html#what-opens-here","l":"deep","x":"PNG, JPG, JPEG, WebP, BMP, TIFF, TGA and DDS files open in the image viewer. Each card shows the format in its corner and a thumbnail. TIFF files with a planar layout are decoded as well as the common uncompressed and LZW kinds. Open a picture with Enter or a double-click. Esc closes it."},{"t":"Images and textures","s":"Moving around","u":"deep/images.html#moving-around","l":"deep","x":"Zoom : mouse wheel, or the zoom buttons. Z and drag zooms too, 0 resets the zoom, and Ctrl + 0 fits the picture to the window. Pan : hold the right mouse button and drag. The left button is reserved for selection. Next and previous : the arrow buttons, or the Left and Right arrow keys, step through the other pictures in the folder. Esc closes the viewer."},{"t":"Images and textures","s":"File information","u":"deep/images.html#file-information","l":"deep","x":"The inspector (press I , see the inspector ) shows the file type, size, resolution, colour, channels and sample type of the picture you have selected."},{"t":"Images and textures","s":"Texture sets","u":"deep/images.html#texture-sets","l":"deep","x":"A material is often saved as several maps that share a base name, such as wood_basecolor.png , wood_normal.png and wood_roughness.png . The grid always shows every file. Choose View as texture set to group the maps of a material into one card. The app recognises the usual names for base colour, normal, roughness, metallic, height and ambient occlusion. If two files could be the same map (for example wood_normal.png and wood_normal.jpg ), no set is offered, so nothing is grouped by mistake. Note: The viewer keeps the file's own pixels. Nothing is resampled or compressed when you look at it."},{"t":"Inspector","s":"Opening it","u":"deep/inspector.html#opening-it","l":"deep","x":"Press I , or click the info button in the top bar. The Inspector opens on the right of the folder. It shows the details of the selected file and updates as you move the selection. Close it with I again or the cross at the top. The Inspector shows the selected file's details below its name"},{"t":"Inspector","s":"What it shows","u":"deep/inspector.html#what-it-shows","l":"deep","x":"The fields depend on the type of file: All files : type, size, date modified and the full path. Images and textures : resolution, colour, channels, sample type and compression. EXR : parts and channels, with the file's layers. Video and audio : duration and media information. Folders : the folder's created and modified dates."},{"t":"Inspector","s":"Resizing","u":"deep/inspector.html#resizing","l":"deep","x":"Drag the left edge of the Inspector to make it wider or narrower. Drag the left edge to make the Inspector wider or narrower Tip: The Inspector and the viewers' own side panels are different. The HDR and EXR viewer, for example, has its own panel with the exposure and tone-mapping controls. See HDR and EXR maps ."},{"t":"Labels and tags","s":"Colour labels","u":"deep/labels-tags.html#colour-labels","l":"deep","x":"There are seven colours: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple and gray. Each card has a small tag button. Click it to open the label panel and choose a colour. A label shows as a stripe on the card's edge and as a small mark on the card, so you can spot it while scrolling. The panel holds the colour swatches and the tags for one file Folders take labels and tags in the same way."},{"t":"Labels and tags","s":"Tags","u":"deep/labels-tags.html#tags","l":"deep","x":"In the Tags part of the panel, type a word and press Enter . Tags are lower case, inner spaces are collapsed, and a tag can be up to 24 characters long. A file can have up to 12 tags. Tags on a card show as small chips, with a count when there are more than fit."},{"t":"Labels and tags","s":"Filtering","u":"deep/labels-tags.html#filtering","l":"deep","x":"The label filter in the top bar lists the colours and the tags used in the folder. Choose one or more and only the matching files stay in view. Clear the filter to see everything again."},{"t":"Labels and tags","s":"Where labels are saved","u":"deep/labels-tags.html#where-labels-are-saved","l":"deep","x":"Labels and tags are saved in file_labels.json , in the app's data folder next to the folder-icon store. Nothing is written inside your folders, so labels do not travel with the files. A file with no colour and no tags loses its entry. Note: Labels are local to this PC. They are not shared with other people or other computers."},{"t":"Markdown documents","s":"Opening a Markdown file","u":"deep/markdown.html#opening-a-markdown-file","l":"deep","x":".md and .markdown files open in a reading page instead of a plain text view. Open one with Enter or a double-click, or press Space in the folder view for a quick look. The viewer only shows the document; it never changes the file. A notes file with a tip, a picture, a table and a task list. The outline of headings is on the right."},{"t":"Markdown documents","s":"What it shows","u":"deep/markdown.html#what-it-shows","l":"deep","x":"Headings, paragraphs, bold , italic , ~~strikethrough~~, quotes and lists. Tables, with the column alignment from the file. Task lists with ticked and empty boxes. Code blocks with colours for common languages (JavaScript, Python, Rust, C and C++, GLSL, MEL, shell, JSON, YAML and more) and a Copy button on each block. Call-outs written as > [!NOTE] , > [!TIP] , > [!IMPORTANT] , > [!WARNING] and > [!CAUTION] . A --- properties block at the top of the file, tucked into a &quot;Document properties&quot; fold. The page follows the colour theme you chose in Settings, so it is light in the Light theme and dark in the others."},{"t":"Markdown documents","s":"Pictures, GIFs and video","u":"deep/markdown.html#pictures-gifs-and-video","l":"deep","x":"Pictures in the document are loaded from where the file says they are: Next to the document. ![](shots/lookdev.png) shows shots\\lookdev.png from the folder the .md file is in. ../ goes up a folder. A full path or a network share. A path such as D:\\Library\\ref.jpg or \\\\studio\\library\\ref.jpg works too, so a document can show files on a network drive. A web address. Pictures from https:// addresses show when you are online. PNG, JPG, WebP and BMP pictures show as they are, and animated GIFs play . Click a picture to see it large, and click again or press Esc to close it. A picture that cannot be found is shown as a small note with its name instead of a broken symbol. <video> and <audio> tags play the file next to the document."},{"t":"Markdown documents","s":"The outline","u":"deep/markdown.html#the-outline","l":"deep","x":"The panel on the right lists the headings. Click one to jump to it; the heading you are reading is highlighted. Press O to hide or show it. In a narrow window the outline hides itself to leave room for the text."},{"t":"Markdown documents","s":"Links","u":"deep/markdown.html#links","l":"deep","x":"A link to a heading in the same document ( #shot-notes ) scrolls to it. A link to another .md file opens it in the viewer. Back in the toolbar (or Backspace ) returns to the document you came from. A web address opens in your browser. A link to any other file or folder opens it with its default program."},{"t":"Markdown documents","s":"Reading comfortably","u":"deep/markdown.html#reading-comfortably","l":"deep","x":"+ and - , or Ctrl + mouse wheel, make the text larger or smaller. Ctrl + 0 goes back to the normal size. The size is remembered. S switches between the formatted page and the Markdown text, which you can select and copy. Page Down and Space , Page Up and Shift + Space , Home , End and the arrow keys scroll. Left and Right open the previous or next Markdown file in the folder. Very large files show their first 2 MB, with a note at the top; Open in the toolbar opens the whole file in your default program."},{"t":"Markdown documents","s":"Safety","u":"deep/markdown.html#safety","l":"deep","x":"A Markdown file is only text and cannot run anything in the app. Scripts, forms, frames and styles inside a document are removed, and links to anything other than web, mail or local files are blocked, so opening a file from someone else is as safe as opening a picture."},{"t":"PDF documents","s":"Opening a PDF","u":"deep/pdf.html#opening-a-pdf","l":"deep","x":"PDF files show their first page as the thumbnail. Open one with Enter or a double-click. The viewer shows the whole document in one column that you can scroll, so you can read a brief or a shot list without a separate reader. Pages scroll in one column. The toolbar holds the page number, zoom and rotation."},{"t":"PDF documents","s":"Moving through the pages","u":"deep/pdf.html#moving-through-the-pages","l":"deep","x":"Page Down or Space goes to the next page, Page Up or Shift + Space to the previous one. Home and End go to the first and last page. Up and Down scroll a little."},{"t":"PDF documents","s":"Zoom and fit","u":"deep/pdf.html#zoom-and-fit","l":"deep","x":"Ctrl + mouse wheel, or + and - , zooms in and out. Ctrl + 0 fits the page width, F fits the whole page, and Ctrl + 1 shows the page at 100%."},{"t":"PDF documents","s":"Rotate and pan","u":"deep/pdf.html#rotate-and-pan","l":"deep","x":"R rotates the page by 90 degrees. Drag with the left mouse button to pan when the page is larger than the window. Left and Right open the previous or next PDF in the folder."},{"t":"Quick Look","s":"Opening and closing","u":"deep/quick-look.html#opening-and-closing","l":"deep","x":"Select a file in the folder view and press Space . A window opens over the grid and shows the file in the viewer it would normally get: an image, a 3D model, an HDR map, a video, an audio file, a PDF, a Markdown document, a render texture or an image sequence. Press Space or Esc to close it. Enter closes the window and opens the file in its full viewer, and double-clicking the picture does the same. Files without a viewer, such as text or archives, are skipped. Quick Look only works in the folder view, not inside a viewer. The window shows the selected texture at a size that fits"},{"t":"Quick Look","s":"Moving through the folder","u":"deep/quick-look.html#moving-through-the-folder","l":"deep","x":"The arrow keys move the selection in the grid, and the window follows the selection. Nothing opens until you press Enter , so you can look through a folder without leaving it. Arrow keys move the selection and the preview follows it"},{"t":"Quick Look","s":"Moving the window","u":"deep/quick-look.html#moving-the-window","l":"deep","x":"Drag the title bar to move the window. It stays on top of the folder and does not block the rest of the grid."},{"t":"Quick Look","s":"Scrubbing video and audio","u":"deep/quick-look.html#scrubbing-video-and-audio","l":"deep","x":"Quick Look is also a quick way to check a clip. Drag along the scrubber under a video and the picture follows your pointer. The video keeps playing while you scrub, so you can find the right moment without opening the full player. Drag the scrubber to move through the clip Audio files can be scrubbed by dragging as well."},{"t":"Render textures (.tx and .tex)","s":"What it is for","u":"deep/render-textures.html#what-it-is-for","l":"deep","x":"Renderers do not read a texture file as it is. Arnold ( .tx ) and RenderMan ( .tex ) convert it first into mip levels, smaller copies used when the object is far from the camera. This viewer shows those levels, so you can check the texture as the renderer will see it. It opens straight onto the In the render tab, and the Texture tab lets you browse the levels."},{"t":"Render textures (.tx and .tex)","s":"The two tabs","u":"deep/render-textures.html#the-two-tabs","l":"deep","x":"Texture : look at the texture itself, one mip level at a time. Wheel zooms and dragging pans. The buttons zoom in and out, and a double-click fits the texture to the screen. In the render : see the texture on the pixels of a final render. Choose the render size (1K, 2K, 3K, 4K or 8K), then slide how much of the frame the object covers, or type a size in pixels, such as 10 pixels. The texture is shown magnified so single pixels are visible."},{"t":"Render textures (.tx and .tex)","s":"The verdict","u":"deep/render-textures.html#the-verdict","l":"deep","x":"The panel gives a plain-words verdict for the current settings: Too soft , A little soft , Sharp enough , More than enough or Overkill . It also says how big the texture needs to be and which mip level the renderer reads. A colour chart shows the verdict for every render size and distance for the open texture. Click a smaller mip level to test a question such as &quot;is 2K enough?&quot;."},{"t":"Render textures (.tx and .tex)","s":"What-if sizes","u":"deep/render-textures.html#what-if-sizes","l":"deep","x":"The texture size comes from the file. A Texture size choice lets you try a bigger size than the file, such as &quot;what if this were 8K?&quot;. The verdict and the chart use that size and say so; the preview keeps showing the file's real pixels."},{"t":"Render textures (.tx and .tex)","s":"Files it cannot read","u":"deep/render-textures.html#files-it-cannot-read","l":"deep","x":"Files based on OpenEXR, or using Pixar's compression, cannot be read here. The viewer says so instead of failing silently. A .tex file that is really a LaTeX document is also reported. Use the left and right arrow keys to move to the next or previous texture in the folder, and Esc to close."},{"t":"Send to apps","s":"Sending a file","u":"deep/send-to-apps.html#sending-a-file","l":"deep","x":"Right-click a file and choose the app under Send to . The file opens in that app. Send to lists the apps you added. Here: Photoshop and Blender."},{"t":"Send to apps","s":"The apps list","u":"deep/send-to-apps.html#the-apps-list","l":"deep","x":"Open Settings and look at External apps . The list starts with the apps the app finds on your PC when it first runs, such as Photoshop or Blender. Removing an app from the list keeps it removed, so it does not come back on the next start. To add one, press Browse , choose the program's .exe , give it a name, and press Add . The app appears in the Send to menu straight away. Scan looks for installed apps again."},{"t":"Settings and themes","s":"Opening Settings","u":"deep/settings-themes.html#opening-settings","l":"deep","x":"Click the gear at the top right, or Studio Preferences & Configuration . The window has five parts. Appearance at the top, then Blender, External apps and the asset cache"},{"t":"Settings and themes","s":"Appearance","u":"deep/settings-themes.html#appearance","l":"deep","x":"Four themes are available. The choice is remembered and applies at once. Theme Look Obsidian Dark The default: neutral dark grey with white accents Dark Gray A softer, lighter grey True Black Pure black, best on OLED screens Light A bright studio look"},{"t":"Settings and themes","s":"Documentation","u":"deep/settings-themes.html#documentation","l":"deep","x":"Open the user guide opens this guide in your default browser. It is the same as the question-mark Help button in the top bar. The guide is built into the app and works without the internet; the first time you open it, the app saves a copy in its data folder and opens that copy."},{"t":"Settings and themes","s":"Blender","u":"deep/settings-themes.html#blender","l":"deep","x":"The Blender Executable Path box shows the Blender the app will use for USD, Alembic and Blender files. The status line under it says whether Blender was found. Use Browse to choose the blender.exe yourself and Save to keep it. See USD, Alembic and Blender ."},{"t":"Settings and themes","s":"External apps","u":"deep/settings-themes.html#external-apps","l":"deep","x":"The list of apps for the Send to menu, with Browse , Add and Scan . See Send to apps ."},{"t":"Settings and themes","s":"Asset cache","u":"deep/settings-themes.html#asset-cache","l":"deep","x":"The cache keeps thumbnails and converted models so folders open fast. The section shows how much space it uses and has a Clear Cache button. Clearing it is safe: the thumbnails and conversions are made again when needed."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"A USD, Alembic or Blender file does not open","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#a-usd-alembic-or-blender-file-does-not-open","l":"deep","x":"Check the sidebar footer. If it says Blender was not found, open Settings and set the Blender path. If Blender is found but the conversion fails, the message names the file. Open the same file in Blender to see whether the file itself is the problem."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"A network share will not open","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#a-network-share-will-not-open","l":"deep","x":"If you see an error that starts with a sign-in message, or Windows error 1272, the share needs a sign-in that File Explorer does not share with this app. Click + next to Network locations, enter the user name and password, and tick Remember . See Network shares . If the share is offline, it stays in the sidebar and comes back when the share does."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"Thumbnails are slow","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#thumbnails-are-slow","l":"deep","x":"The first visit to a folder decodes every image and EXR. Large multi-layer EXR files take the longest. The result is saved in the cache, so later visits are fast."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"A render texture shows a message","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#a-render-texture-shows-a-message","l":"deep","x":".tx and .tex files that are based on OpenEXR, or that use Pixar compression, cannot be read here. The message says so. See Render textures ."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"Quick Look does not open","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#quick-look-does-not-open","l":"deep","x":"Quick Look needs the folder view, a file selected and a focus outside text boxes. Press Esc to leave the address box first. Files with no viewer, such as text, are skipped."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"Keys do nothing","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#keys-do-nothing","l":"deep","x":"The address box and any open dialog take the keys first. Press Esc to close the box or the dialog, then try again."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"I deleted something by accident","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#i-deleted-something-by-accident","l":"deep","x":"Delete moves files to the Recycle Bin, so restore them from there. Only Shift + Delete removes files for good, and it asks you to type DELETE to confirm."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"Something else","u":"deep/troubleshooting.html#something-else","l":"deep","x":"Open an issue on the project's GitHub page with the file type, what you clicked and the message on screen."},{"t":"USD, Alembic and Blender files","s":"How the conversion works","u":"deep/usd-outliner.html#how-the-conversion-works","l":"deep","x":"The app cannot read USD, Alembic ( .abc ) or Blender ( .blend ) files directly. It starts Blender in the background, without its interface, and exports a .glb copy of the scene. The copy is kept in the cache, so the second open is immediate. The sidebar footer shows Blender ABC/USD with a status: Ready when Blender is found, or a message when it is not. Blender 4.x and 5.x are supported. Blender is found automatically in the usual install folders and Steam libraries on each drive. If it is installed somewhere else, set the path in Settings . Press O to show the outliner. It lists the prims of the scene."},{"t":"USD, Alembic and Blender files","s":"The outliner","u":"deep/usd-outliner.html#the-outliner","l":"deep","x":"The outliner is the tree of the scene. Click a line to select that part, and the viewer frames it. The search box at the top filters the names. The eye button on a row hides that part in the viewer without removing it from the tree, which helps when a scene has a cluttered background."},{"t":"USD, Alembic and Blender files","s":"When a file does not open","u":"deep/usd-outliner.html#when-a-file-does-not-open","l":"deep","x":"The status says Blender was not found: set the Blender path in Settings, then open the file again. The conversion fails: the message names the file. Open the same file in Blender to see whether it is a problem with the file itself. The model is huge: the first conversion can take a minute. Later opens use the cache. Note: Converted copies are cached in the app's cache folder. Clear the cache in Settings if you want to free the space."},{"t":"Video and audio","s":"Video","u":"deep/video-and-audio.html#video","l":"deep","x":"MP4, MOV, WebM, MKV and AVI files open in the video player. The bar under the picture has a scrubber, a frame counter (click it to switch between frames and timecode), play and pause, and a speed control. The frame counter switches between frame numbers and timecode when you click it. Step frames : the arrow keys or , and . step one frame at a time. Loop : set an in point with [ or I and an out point with ] or O . The clip then loops between them. \\ clears the loop. Safe areas : turn on the action-safe (90%) and title-safe (80%) guides, and the aspect-ratio guides, for checking framing. Fit : choose how the video fits the window, and reveal the file in Explorer from the same bar. Next and previous : move to the next or previous video in the folder. You can also drag the scrubber in Quick Look, and the video keeps playing while you scrub. See Quick Look ."},{"t":"Video and audio","s":"Audio","u":"deep/video-and-audio.html#audio","l":"deep","x":"WAV, MP3, OGG, FLAC, AAC, AIFF and M4A open in the audio player, with a waveform and the file properties. The waveform shows the level over the whole file. Seamless loop ( L ) repeats the file without a gap, which is useful for checking game loops. Pitch changes the pitch in semitones without changing the speed. Click the value to reset it to 0. Previous and next move through the folder; stop returns to the start."},{"t":"CG Artist File Browser guide","s":"","u":"index.html","l":"home","x":"Quick start Show me the surface A short tour with pictures and animated clips, a keyboard card, and \"How do I…\" answers. Deep dive I want the details One page per feature: image and HDR viewers, 3D and USD, video and audio, compare, labels, settings and troubleshooting."},{"t":"CG Artist File Browser guide","s":"What the app does","u":"index.html#what-the-app-does","l":"home","x":"CG Artist File Browser is a Windows file browser for the files a 3D or VFX artist opens all day. You point it at a folder and it shows the files as pictures: 3D models turn in a viewer, HDR and EXR maps open as a 360° sky with exposure controls, textures can be compared side by side, and video, audio, PDF, Markdown notes and render textures ( .tx , .tex ) open right where you are. Nothing is uploaded anywhere."},{"t":"CG Artist File Browser guide","s":"Start in a minute","u":"index.html#start-in-a-minute","l":"home","x":"Open a folder from the sidebar, or press Ctrl + L and type a path such as D:\\Projects\\Shot_010 . Click a file once to select it, press Space to preview it in a floating window, or double-click to open it fully. Press ? at any time to see every keyboard shortcut. Press / anywhere in this guide to search it."},{"t":"CG Artist File Browser guide","s":"Which level should I read?","u":"index.html#which-level-should-i-read","l":"home","x":"Quick start is for everyday use: what a screen does, how to do a common task, and the keys you need most. Deep dive has one page per feature, with every option, the file formats it understands and what to do when something looks wrong. Each page has a link to the other level when there is one, and the Quick start / Deep dive switch at the top moves between them."},{"t":"CG Artist File Browser guide","s":"About the pictures","u":"index.html#about-the-pictures","l":"home","x":"The screenshots and animated clips in this guide were captured from a browser build of the app with sample files, not from the installed Windows app. They show the same screens and controls. Their file names are stable, so a real screenshot can replace one by copying a file over it. See the FAQ for more."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Open a folder or a network share","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#open-a-folder-or-a-network-share","l":"quick","x":"Click a drive in the sidebar, or press Ctrl + L and type the path. For a share, type it like File Explorer does, for example \\\\mypc\\library . Shares you open are kept in the sidebar. If Windows will not let the app in, use the + next to Network locations to sign in. Folders and network drives explains the details."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Preview a file without leaving the folder","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#preview-a-file-without-leaving-the-folder","l":"quick","x":"Select it and press Space . Arrow keys move on, and Esc or Space closes the window. Quick Look covers video scrubbing and moving the window."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Open a file in its full viewer","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#open-a-file-in-its-full-viewer","l":"quick","x":"Double-click it, or select it and press Enter ."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Look at a 3D model","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#look-at-a-3d-model","l":"quick","x":"Open a .glb , .obj , .fbx , .stl or .ply file. Drag with the left mouse button to orbit, the right button to pan and the wheel to zoom. Press F to frame the model. 3D models lists the shading, light and camera options."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Open a USD or Alembic file","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#open-a-usd-or-alembic-file","l":"quick","x":"Install Blender, then check the path in Settings. The app converts .usd , .abc and .blend files to a model in the background and keeps the result. USD and Alembic explains what to expect."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Read a Markdown note or README","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#read-a-markdown-note-or-readme","l":"quick","x":"Open the .md file. Pictures and GIFs next to it show in the page, the outline on the right jumps between headings, and S shows the plain text. Markdown documents covers links, network drives and the keys."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Read an HDR or EXR map","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#read-an-hdr-or-exr-map","l":"quick","x":"Open it. It appears as a 360° sky. Hold E and drag to change the exposure, and use the tone-mapping list in the panel on the right to change how the image is squeezed onto the screen. HDR and EXR has the rest."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Compare two versions of a render","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#compare-two-versions-of-a-render","l":"quick","x":"Press A on one card and B on the other, then press Compare . Press 1 to 4 to change the mode. Compare covers all of them."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Add a colour label or a tag","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#add-a-colour-label-or-a-tag","l":"quick","x":"Click the small tag button on a card, pick a colour, or type a tag and press Enter . To see only labelled files, use the label filter in the top bar. Labels and tags explains where they are saved."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Change a folder's icon","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#change-a-folders-icon","l":"quick","x":"Right-click the folder, choose Change icon… , and pick one from the library or import your own PNG, SVG, ICO, WebP or JPG. Folders and network drives has the details."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Convert a batch of images","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#convert-a-batch-of-images","l":"quick","x":"Select the images, right-click one of them and choose Convert… . Pick the format and the output folder. Existing files are never overwritten. Batch converter lists the formats."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Send a file to another app","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#send-a-file-to-another-app","l":"quick","x":"Right-click the file and use Send to . The apps come from Settings, where you can add or remove them. Send to apps explains how to add one."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Delete or rename a file","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#delete-or-rename-a-file","l":"quick","x":"Press F2 to rename. Press Delete to move the selection to the Recycle Bin after a confirmation. Shift + Delete removes it for good. The app never deletes a drive or a share root."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Change the look","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#change-the-look","l":"quick","x":"Open Settings (the gear, top right) and choose a theme under Appearance. Settings and themes lists the four options."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Find a shortcut","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#find-a-shortcut","l":"quick","x":"Press ? , or open the keyboard shortcut card and type what you want to do."},{"t":"How do I…?","s":"Open this guide from the app","u":"quick/how-do-i.html#open-this-guide-from-the-app","l":"quick","x":"Click the question-mark Help button in the top bar. The guide opens in your default browser and works offline. It is also under Documentation in Settings and at the bottom of the shortcut card. Settings and themes has the details."},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"","u":"quick/shortcuts.html","l":"quick","x":"Press ? or F1 in the app to see the same list. The question-mark Help button in the top bar opens this whole guide in your browser (no key is needed for it). The list below is generated from the source, so it matches what the app does. The card in the app. Press Esc to close it. Find a shortcut 99 shortcuts"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Folders and selection","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#folders-and-selection","l":"quick","x":"Arrow keys Move the selection (up and down move a row) Shift + Arrow keys Extend the selection from the anchor item Home or End First / last item Page Up or Page Down Move a screen at a time Enter Open the selected folder or file Backspace or Alt + Up Go up to the parent folder Alt + Left or Alt + Right Back / forward through folder history Mouse back or Mouse forward Side buttons on the mouse: back / forward Ctrl + L or Alt + D Type a folder path or network address Ctrl + F Type in the filter box (top right) Delete Delete the selected files and folders: moved to the Recycle Bin after a confirm Shift + Delete Delete the selection for good, skipping the Recycle Bin (type DELETE to confirm) F2 Rename the selected item (one item at a time) Ctrl + C Copy the selected files and folders (File Explorer can paste them too) Ctrl + X Cut the selected files and folders (they move when you paste) Ctrl + V Paste into this folder: names already taken get a number, or you can choose Replace Ctrl + Shift + N Make a new folder here and name it Ctrl + Shift + C Copy the path of the selected item (one path per line for a selection) F5 or Ctrl + R Refresh this folder in place (same folder, selection and view) Ctrl + A Select all Right-click Menu for the item, or on empty space: Refresh, Paste, New folder Click Select one item Ctrl + Click Add or remove one item Shift + Click Select a range Ctrl + "},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Inspector drawer","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#inspector-drawer","l":"quick","x":"I or Alt + Enter Show or hide the Inspector: details of the selected file, beside the grid"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Any viewer","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#any-viewer","l":"quick","x":"Esc Close the viewer (leaves full screen first)"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Quick Look","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#quick-look","l":"quick","x":"Space Open the selected file in a small floating preview (audio and video start playing) Space or Esc Close the floating preview Arrow keys While the preview is open, move through the folder and the preview follows Double-click Open the file in the full viewer (also from the floating preview)"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Image and texture viewers","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#image-and-texture-viewers","l":"quick","x":"Left or Right Previous / next image or texture Z + Drag Zoom: hold Z and drag (image viewer) Ctrl + 0 Fit to screen (or hold Z and press 0)"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Video and image sequences","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#video-and-image-sequences","l":"quick","x":"Space Play / pause Left or Right or , or . Step one frame back / forward (Shift + Left / Right: one second) Home or End First / last frame (image sequences) I or [ Set the in point of the loop O or ] Set the out point of the loop \\ Clear the loop S Snapshot the current frame F Full screen 1 – 6 Show RGB, R, G, B, alpha or luminance only C Cycle through the channel views E + Drag Exposure: hold E and drag E + + or E + - Step exposure by 0.5 while E is held E + 0 Reset exposure while E is held Z + Drag Zoom: hold Z and drag Z + 0 Reset zoom while Z is held"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Audio player","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#audio-player","l":"quick","x":"Space Play / pause Left or Right Back / forward 5 seconds L Loop on / off"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"PDF viewer","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#pdf-viewer","l":"quick","x":"Page Down or Space Next page Page Up or Shift + Space Previous page Home or End First / last page Up or Down Scroll a little Left or Right Previous / next file + or - Zoom in / out Ctrl + 0 Fit width Ctrl + 1 Actual size (100%) F Fit page R Rotate 90 degrees"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Markdown viewer","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#markdown-viewer","l":"quick","x":"Page Down or Space Scroll down a screen Page Up or Shift + Space Scroll up a screen Home or End Top / bottom of the document Up or Down Scroll a little Left or Right Previous / next Markdown file in the folder Backspace Back to the document you followed a link from + or - Larger / smaller text (also Ctrl + mouse wheel) Ctrl + 0 Reset the text size O Show / hide the outline of headings S Switch between the formatted page and the Markdown text"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"3D model viewer","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#3d-model-viewer","l":"quick","x":"F Frame the model O Show / hide the outliner (prim tree; click a prim to select and frame it) Numpad 1 or Numpad 3 or Numpad 7 Front, right or top view (Ctrl: back or left for 1 and 3) Numpad 5 Toggle orthographic view"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"HDR and EXR inspector","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#hdr-and-exr-inspector","l":"quick","x":"Z + Drag Zoom: hold Z and drag 0 Reset zoom E + Drag Exposure: hold E and drag E + + or E + - Step exposure by 0.5 while E is held E + 0 Reset exposure while E is held V Flip vertically F Fit view W Wipe on / off P Probes on / off I or N Show / hide the sidebar"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Compare","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#compare","l":"quick","x":"Space Switch between A and B (images and 3D models) X Switch between A and B (video) 1 or 2 or 3 or 4 Wipe, split, toggle and diff modes (4 is not for 3D models) R Reset the view (F also does it for 3D models) Space Play / pause the video compare Left or Right Step one frame in the video compare (Shift: one second) Home Back to the start of the video compare"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"Menus and the address box","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#menus-and-the-address-box","l":"quick","x":"Enter Go to the path typed in the address box (Esc cancels) Esc Close the sort, context, label or icon menu"},{"t":"Keyboard shortcuts","s":"This list","u":"quick/shortcuts.html#this-list","l":"quick","x":"? or F1 Show or hide this list Esc Close this list No shortcut matches. Try a shorter word, or search the whole guide with / ."},{"t":"A quick tour","s":"The main screen","u":"quick/tour.html#the-main-screen","l":"quick","x":"A folder of models. The sidebar lists drives, network locations, recent and pinned folders. Sidebar, left. Drives and network shares, recent folders, pinned folders, and the assets you starred. The box at the bottom counts the files in the current folder. Path bar, top. Where you are, with back, forward and up buttons. Click the empty part of the path, or press Ctrl + L , to type a path. Filter box, top right. Type to narrow the folder to matching names. The type buttons next to it show only 3D, HDR, images, video, audio, PDF or Markdown files. Views. Thumbnails by default. The list icon switches to a details list with name, date, type and size. Your choice is remembered. Details view: click a column header to sort"},{"t":"A quick tour","s":"Preview without opening: Quick Look","u":"quick/tour.html#preview-without-opening-quick-look","l":"quick","x":"Select a file and press Space . A small window opens over the folder and shows the file in its own viewer. Press the arrow keys to move through the folder; the window follows. Space or Esc closes it, Enter opens the full viewer. Quick Look shows a texture without leaving the folder Arrow keys move the selection, and the preview follows"},{"t":"A quick tour","s":"Select several files","u":"quick/tour.html#select-several-files","l":"quick","x":"Click picks one file. Ctrl + Click adds or removes one, Shift + Click selects a range, and dragging on empty space draws a box. Ctrl + A selects everything. The status bar at the bottom says how many are selected and their total size. Ctrl + Click and Shift + Click build up a selection"},{"t":"A quick tour","s":"Right-click for actions","u":"quick/tour.html#right-click-for-actions","l":"quick","x":"Right-click a file or folder for its menu: open, reveal in Explorer, copy the path, rename, delete, send to an app, add it to favourites, label it, or convert images. The menu changes with the file type. Send to shows the apps you added in Settings."},{"t":"A quick tour","s":"Compare two files","u":"quick/tour.html#compare-two-files","l":"quick","x":"Each card has an A and a B button. Pick two files, then press Compare in the bar at the bottom. Drag the divider to wipe between them, or use the modes in the top bar. Pick slot A and slot B, then press Compare The wipe divider shows how the two versions differ"},{"t":"A quick tour","s":"Next steps","u":"quick/tour.html#next-steps","l":"quick","x":"How do I…? answers the common tasks in one line each. Keyboard shortcuts lists every key, with a search box. When you want the detail behind a screen, the deep dive has a page for each feature."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Does the app upload my files anywhere?","u":"shared/faq.html#does-the-app-upload-my-files-anywhere","l":"shared","x":"No. Everything is read and shown on your PC. The only network traffic is what Windows itself does when you open a network share, and the Blender conversion runs locally."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Does it change my files?","u":"shared/faq.html#does-it-change-my-files","l":"shared","x":"It only changes what you ask it to. Renaming, deleting (to the Recycle Bin), converting images and sending files to apps all happen when you do them. Labels, tags, favourites and folder icons are stored by the app in its own settings and label files, not inside your folders."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Which Windows versions and processors?","u":"shared/faq.html#which-windows-versions-and-processors","l":"shared","x":"Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit. WebView2 is needed; it is already installed on most Windows 10 and 11 PCs. Linux and macOS are not supported at the moment."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Why do the thumbnails take a moment the first time?","u":"shared/faq.html#why-do-the-thumbnails-take-a-moment-the-first-time","l":"shared","x":"The first time a folder is opened, each image and EXR is decoded. The result is saved in the thumbnail cache, so the next visit is instant. Very large multi-layer EXR files take the longest. See Troubleshooting ."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Where is this guide, and does it need the internet?","u":"shared/faq.html#where-is-this-guide-and-does-it-need-the-internet","l":"shared","x":"The guide is built into the app, so it works offline and is the same in the installed app and the portable exe. Click the question-mark Help button in the top bar, or Open the user guide under Documentation in Settings or at the bottom of the shortcut card ( ? or F1 ). It opens in your default browser. If the browser cannot be started, the app shows the folder where the guide is saved so you can open index.html yourself."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Where are the settings and the cache?","u":"shared/faq.html#where-are-the-settings-and-the-cache","l":"shared","x":"Settings (the Blender path, send-to apps, favourites, recent folders and network sign-ins) are kept in the app's settings file, studio_config.json . Labels are kept in file_labels.json . Thumbnails and converted models are kept in the AssetStudioCache folder under %APPDATA% . Settings has a button to clear the cache."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Can I change the shortcuts?","u":"shared/faq.html#can-i-change-the-shortcuts","l":"shared","x":"The keys are fixed in this version. The shortcut card lists them all."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Is it free?","u":"shared/faq.html#is-it-free","l":"shared","x":"The app is released under the MIT licence. The source and the releases are on the project's GitHub page."},{"t":"FAQ","s":"Why are some screenshots not from my PC?","u":"shared/faq.html#why-are-some-screenshots-not-from-my-pc","l":"shared","x":"The pictures in this guide were captured from a browser build with sample files so that the guide could be made before the Windows build was run. They show the same controls. Real screenshots can replace them by copying files over the old ones."},{"t":"Release notes","s":"","u":"shared/release-notes.html","l":"shared","x":"The current version is 1.17.0 . This list groups the changes by what you see in the app. Version numbers for each release are in the project's history on GitHub."},{"t":"Release notes","s":"Folders, network and navigation","u":"shared/release-notes.html#folders-network-and-navigation","l":"shared","x":"Folder navigation with a history, back and forward, and the mouse side buttons. Mapped and typed network shares in the sidebar, with sign-in for shares that refuse guest access. Saved sign-ins reconnect when the app starts. Recent folders, pinned folders and starred files in the sidebar. A details view like File Explorer's, with sortable columns. In-place refresh with F5 , Ctrl + R and the header button; the selection and view stay."},{"t":"Release notes","s":"Viewers","u":"shared/release-notes.html#viewers","l":"shared","x":"3D viewer with lighting presets, shading modes, matcaps, wireframe, cameras and turntable. USD, Alembic and Blender files converted in the background with Blender, plus a 3D model outliner. HDR and EXR inspector with a 360° view, exposure, tone mapping, channel solo, eyedropper and probes. Render textures ( .tx , .tex ) with mip levels and a &quot;sharp enough?&quot; check. Image sequences that play as one sequence, PDF viewing, video and audio players. Markdown ( .md ) documents in a clean reading page, with pictures and animated GIFs from next to the file or from a network drive, tables, code blocks, task lists, links and a heading outline. Compare with wipe, side-by-side, A/B toggle and diff, for pictures, videos and 3D models."},{"t":"Release notes","s":"Browsing and working with files","u":"shared/release-notes.html#browsing-and-working-with-files","l":"shared","x":"Multi-select with Ctrl and Shift , box selection, and a right-click menu. Quick Look with Space : a floating preview that follows the arrow keys and can scrub video. Colour labels and tags for files and folders, with a label filter. Custom folder icons from a CG library, plus your own PNG, SVG, ICO, WebP and JPG files. Send to apps from the right-click menu. Batch conversion of images to PNG, JPG, TIFF, BMP, TGA and WebP, without overwriting files. Delete to the Recycle Bin, with a confirmation; permanent delete only on Shift + Delete . Keyboard shortcut card on ? and F1 . A Help button in the top bar (and a Documentation entry in Settings) that opens this guide in your browser. The guide is built into the app and works offline."},{"t":"Release notes","s":"Speed and stability","u":"shared/release-notes.html#speed-and-stability","l":"shared","x":"Faster and non-freezing thumbnails for large multi-layer EXR files. Grid virtualisation for large folders. Thumbnail cache with a clear button in Settings."},{"t":"Release notes","s":"Looks","u":"shared/release-notes.html#looks","l":"shared","x":"Four colour themes: Obsidian Dark, Dark Gray, True Black and Light. Inspector drawer that can be resized by dragging its edge."}];
